Third-party tools

The MIT license above covers ONLY the original jddlab code in this repository:
the launcher scripts (`jddlab`, `jddlab.cmd`), the installation/build scripts
under `scripts/`, the MCP server under `mcp/`, and the AI skills under `skills/`.

jddlab is a "pack" that downloads and bundles many independent third-party
reverse-engineering tools into a Docker image. Each bundled tool (Apktool, jadx,
Ghidra, dex2jar, FernFlower, Vineflower, Procyon, Krakatau, APKEditor, APKscan,
Enjarify, Simplify, java-deobfuscator, androguard, objection, android-unpinner,
apk-patcher, smali/baksmali, the Android SDK build-tools, and others) is
distributed under its own license and remains the property of its respective
authors. Those licenses are NOT superseded by this file.

The version and upstream project URL of every bundled tool is recorded inside
the image at `/usr/local/jddlab/software-list.txt` (see `jddlab versions`) and
in each GitHub release. Consult each upstream project for its exact license
terms before redistributing or using it in a commercial context.
